WEBVTT

00:02.440 --> 00:05.230
Good work today, everyone.

00:05.230 --> 00:06.650
Cheers!

00:10.560 --> 00:13.610
Nothing beats a post-raid drink!

00:13.610 --> 00:15.670
I'm glad to hear it.

00:15.670 --> 00:18.230
Does alcohol really taste that good?

00:18.230 --> 00:21.930
If you're curious, why don't you try a sip?

00:23.360 --> 00:28.900
<i>I've never heard of a homunculus 
drinking before. Will she be all right?</i>

00:30.330 --> 00:34.970
I want a sip, I want a sip, I want a sip.

00:32.460 --> 00:34.970
Uh, well, I guess a little can't hurt.

00:35.870 --> 00:37.050
Thank you.

00:42.410 --> 00:43.580
It's so bitter.

00:46.340 --> 00:48.800
It's an acquired taste.

00:48.800 --> 00:51.070
Then, why did you offer me some?

00:53.120 --> 00:56.010
Because it meant 
I got to see that reaction.

00:56.010 --> 00:59.030
The more you drink, the better it tastes.

00:59.030 --> 01:04.910
But y'know, you, Lilia, and Lily 
have been awfully close lately.

01:05.310 --> 01:08.420
Wh-What? I don't think anything's changed.

01:08.710 --> 01:11.640
No? What do you think, Luna?

01:11.640 --> 01:13.920
Hey, don't drag Luna into it.

01:14.960 --> 01:17.670
I think they've gotten closer.

01:17.670 --> 01:19.850
Did that sip get you drunk?

01:20.580 --> 01:25.560
Well, uh, they may not be clan members, 
but they've been helping us a lot.

01:25.560 --> 01:29.550
I'm just worried 
we might be imposing on them.

01:29.550 --> 01:32.690
So you're <i>not</i> more than just party mates?

01:33.000 --> 01:34.710
Definitely not.

01:34.710 --> 01:37.570
Huh. In that case...

01:38.450 --> 01:41.860
Why don't you and I become 
<i>more</i> than just party mates?

01:44.320 --> 01:46.400
Are you drunk?

01:46.400 --> 01:48.130
Hm, maybe?

01:50.660 --> 01:54.510
I've said it before, 
but things like that aren't on my mind.

01:55.090 --> 01:59.040
For now, raiding 
labyrinths is my priority,

01:59.040 --> 02:03.120
so I don't intend on getting into that 
kind of relationship with anyone just yet.

02:03.120 --> 02:06.430
Then, you'll have to address
 all of that stuff first.

02:06.890 --> 02:11.620
Master, does that mean 
you're not dating anyone right now?

02:11.620 --> 02:13.310
Hm? Uh, I guess not.

02:16.550 --> 02:17.410
What is it?

02:18.100 --> 02:25.830
I have so much fun whenever I'm with you,
 and I get this warm feeling in my chest.

02:26.270 --> 02:30.290
I'd like to spend even more 
time with you, Master.

02:30.290 --> 02:32.580
What? Uh, sure.

02:32.580 --> 02:34.930
Well, look at you, Mister Popular.

02:34.930 --> 02:36.260
Shut up.

02:38.510 --> 02:39.720
Um...

02:40.030 --> 02:41.850
Should we ask for some water?

02:43.050 --> 02:45.190
Ah, Luna! Are you okay?

02:44.390 --> 02:47.020
I see trouble in your future.

02:45.190 --> 02:47.560
You're totally hammered.

02:50.150 --> 02:52.310
What an exhausting day.

02:57.400 --> 02:58.990
What? Wait...

03:00.000 --> 03:01.100
Lilia?

03:14.000 --> 03:23.840
<b>The Strongest Tank's Labyrinth Raids</b>

03:14.000 --> 03:23.840
<b>Labyrinth Raids</b>

03:14.000 --> 03:23.840
m 124 277 l 134 267 140 274 144 272 150 275 163 260 177 271 472 271 488 261 502 275 507 270 510 274 518 267 528 277 516 288 526 298 517 306 510 299 506 304 500 299 489 312 473 302 178 302 163 313 150 300 146 303 140 299 134 306 125 297 134 287

03:14.000 --> 03:23.840
A Tank with a Rare 9,999 Resistance Skill 
Got Kicked from the Hero's Party

04:35.060 --> 04:36.120
Lilia?

04:38.590 --> 04:40.420
Welcome back, Rud.

04:40.700 --> 04:43.880
Why are you sleeping in my bed?

04:43.880 --> 04:45.940
Oh, right.

04:46.390 --> 04:49.140
I wanted to ask you about something.

04:49.140 --> 04:52.250
I had Marius let me into your room
 so I could wait for you.

04:51.680 --> 04:53.850
<b>Thanks 
for 
holding 
down 
the 
fort</b>

04:52.250 --> 04:53.850
Thanks for holding down the fort.

04:54.480 --> 04:57.060
I guess I was more tired than I realized.

04:57.530 --> 05:01.150
I see. So what did you want to talk about?

05:02.640 --> 05:04.390
Lily's behavior today.

05:05.580 --> 05:08.320
She worked really hard today.

05:09.000 --> 05:14.330
Yeah. Honestly, Lily surprised me.
She can do more than I thought.

05:15.290 --> 05:19.170
She's always been able to get things done 
as long as she stays calm. It was easy for her.

05:19.650 --> 05:23.760
You're twins, after all. It makes sense 
that your abilities are comparable.

05:24.700 --> 05:28.860
Lily put in a lot of effort today. 
She wants to change, little by little.

05:29.440 --> 05:32.490
Though it seems like 
she exhausted herself by trying too hard.

05:34.000 --> 05:34.840
What's wrong?

05:35.650 --> 05:38.680
What do you think about change?

05:38.680 --> 05:40.690
Has it ever scared you?

05:41.440 --> 05:46.390
I guess so. I actually don't 
like change all that much.

05:46.390 --> 05:50.010
Especially not what's been 
happening to Avancia recently.

05:51.150 --> 05:53.580
Sometimes, I feel it'd be better
 if things didn't change.

05:54.320 --> 05:57.490
I'm sure a lot of the townsfolk feel the same.

05:58.360 --> 06:01.750
Even I don't know if 
we're doing the right thing.

06:02.840 --> 06:06.060
But I'm also kind of glad 
that things have changed.

06:07.840 --> 06:11.980
Avancia would never have gotten
so lively if it hadn't changed.

06:13.590 --> 06:17.890
So I think the best option is 
to find a way to enjoy change.

06:18.980 --> 06:25.110
I thought it'd be best if things 
stayed the same, and I still do.

06:25.620 --> 06:29.200
Honestly, I'm weaker than Lily.

06:29.200 --> 06:31.930
Naturally, I want to support her.

06:32.900 --> 06:36.920
But I'm also sad to see 
her drift away from me.

06:37.540 --> 06:39.860
<i>Lilia's inability to let her sister go</i>

06:39.860 --> 06:44.000
<i>might be a bigger problem than 
Lily's desire to become independent.</i>

06:44.500 --> 06:46.040
Some things will change,

06:46.900 --> 06:50.460
but I'm sure "Lilia and Lily" won't.

06:50.460 --> 06:51.120
What?

06:51.990 --> 06:55.020
I think you two will always 
get along and stay together.

06:55.020 --> 06:59.180
Even if stuff changes, 
that core principle will remain the same.

07:00.010 --> 07:04.710
So even if something changes, you two will 
likely continue to live together like always.

07:07.010 --> 07:09.570
You've thought about that 
more than I was expecting.

07:09.990 --> 07:12.920
Sorry that all I have to offer 
are my own thoughts.

07:12.920 --> 07:16.030
It's fine. That's what 
I wanted to hear anyway.

07:16.760 --> 07:22.030
Lily was so brilliant today. 
I couldn't look at her, but...

07:23.060 --> 07:26.920
But starting tomorrow, 
I don't want to turn away.

07:28.500 --> 07:29.680
Good luck.

07:32.440 --> 07:33.630
I'll do my best.

07:37.800 --> 07:43.310
<b>Keild Labyrinth: 1st Floor</b>

07:37.850 --> 07:43.310
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

07:39.300 --> 07:42.320
We'll start on the 51st floor today.

07:42.320 --> 07:43.310
Go ahead, Lily.

07:43.590 --> 07:47.650
Okay. The 51st floor is as far as 
the two major clans have reached,

07:47.650 --> 07:49.690
so we don't have a lot of info on it.

07:49.690 --> 07:52.320
But because the fog in 
the labyrinth is so dense,

07:52.320 --> 07:55.870
we may need to use something other 
than detection magic to find monsters.

07:57.050 --> 07:59.770
Lily, you'll remain in charge of detection.

07:59.770 --> 08:02.150
Marius and I will search as much as we can.

08:02.610 --> 08:04.140
Luna, be on your guard, too.

08:04.140 --> 08:09.650
Uh, um, I-I didn't mean anything 
by what I said yesterday!

08:09.650 --> 08:10.740
Huh? Uh, right.

08:10.740 --> 08:14.470
So you're the type who remembers 
what they did while drunk, huh?

08:14.920 --> 08:17.680
Looks like we're all ready.

08:18.300 --> 08:19.720
Dungeon Walk.

08:20.850 --> 08:24.850
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

08:20.850 --> 08:24.850
<b>Keild Labyrinth: 51st Floor</b>

08:25.570 --> 08:28.530
Yup, the fog is rather dense in here.

08:28.530 --> 08:31.570
Like I thought, 
my detection spell isn't working.

08:32.070 --> 08:35.780
Luna, can you try clearing 
the fog with a wind spell?

08:35.780 --> 08:36.780
Right.

08:42.800 --> 08:43.920
That didn't work.

08:43.920 --> 08:47.260
This fog is probably made of mana.

08:48.010 --> 08:50.620
That's why the wind couldn't clear it.

08:51.060 --> 08:55.860
But since monsters also have mana,
 we can focus on that.

08:56.790 --> 08:57.840
I'll give it a shot.

09:01.540 --> 09:04.310
<i>It's not perfect, 
but I can tell where they are.</i>

09:07.150 --> 09:07.850
<i>Incoming.</i>

09:08.380 --> 09:10.630
Stand back, everyone. 
There's something out there.

09:11.540 --> 09:12.650
Provoke.

09:17.720 --> 09:19.120
<i>Is this water magic?</i>

09:21.360 --> 09:24.250
They're probably sahagin.

09:24.570 --> 09:25.710
I'll scatter them.

09:31.040 --> 09:34.010
It's annoying how this fog 
is obscuring the enemy.

09:40.000 --> 09:44.340
Guys, flee toward my ten o'clock. 
They haven't completely surrounded us.

09:45.420 --> 09:46.700
It's all you.

09:47.190 --> 09:48.520
Provoke.

09:52.440 --> 09:54.150
<i>They've finally shown themselves.</i>

09:54.760 --> 09:57.610
<i>Like Lily said, they're sahagin.</i>

10:06.700 --> 10:10.540
I'm so good at detecting, 
I can act even if I'm blinded.

10:10.990 --> 10:12.170
Nice, Marius.

10:14.000 --> 10:18.920
<i>We learned to detect the 
monster's mana like Marius suggested,</i>

10:18.920 --> 10:22.100
<i>and successfully defeated the sahagin
 that appeared after that.</i>

10:24.480 --> 10:27.100
Let's take a break before 
heading to the next floor.

10:27.370 --> 10:29.480
Okay, I'll make us something to eat.

10:29.480 --> 10:31.060
We'll help.

10:33.520 --> 10:36.180
We're going to eat the sahagin?

10:36.180 --> 10:38.800
Yeah. We need to eat while we can.

10:40.710 --> 10:44.910
But man, the materials 
that dropped are amazing.

10:45.170 --> 10:48.370
Right? It's all top-class stuff.

10:49.510 --> 10:54.840
Because of our conversation, 
I've had no trouble looking at Lily today.

10:56.180 --> 10:57.550
Thanks.

10:59.550 --> 11:02.200
Food's ready, you two.

11:02.200 --> 11:03.760
These sahagin are delicious.

11:10.010 --> 11:12.400
There's no fog, but this place is huge.

11:12.400 --> 11:14.130
It's like a boss room.

11:14.130 --> 11:16.150
Something's coming.

11:18.040 --> 11:19.100
A magic circle?

11:23.200 --> 11:24.870
It's a dark skeleton!

11:26.150 --> 11:27.660
Something else is spawning!

11:31.310 --> 11:33.250
I've never seen those before.

11:33.250 --> 11:35.240
Blue, red, yellow.

11:35.240 --> 11:37.630
They look like crystals.

11:38.200 --> 11:39.840
Shield of Sacrifice.

11:42.560 --> 11:44.490
<i>Such incredible pressure.</i>

11:44.490 --> 11:47.510
<i>The monsters we've fought 
up to now don't even compare.</i>

11:48.120 --> 11:51.940
Lily, command us. 
I'm going to start by charging it.

11:52.730 --> 11:53.480
Got it.

11:53.950 --> 11:55.690
Provoke.

11:58.820 --> 11:59.650
What the...

12:00.250 --> 12:01.480
It's one of the crystals.

12:01.480 --> 12:06.370
The yellow crystal created something 
like a barrier when you attacked.

12:06.760 --> 12:09.780
<i>This is obnoxious. I'll pull back for now.</i>

12:13.790 --> 12:15.710
<i>So the red one attacks, huh?</i>

12:19.430 --> 12:20.840
<i>And the blue one?</i>

12:22.480 --> 12:24.130
<i>It got faster?</i>

12:25.920 --> 12:26.850
<i>I get it now.</i>

12:27.450 --> 12:30.530
<i>The yellow crystal acts like a tank, 
the blue one casts enhancing magic,</i>

12:30.530 --> 12:33.030
<i>and the red one casts offensive spells.</i>

12:33.030 --> 12:34.810
<i>What an annoying monster.</i>

12:35.390 --> 12:38.270
<i>That yellow crystal barrier 
is especially problematic.</i>

12:38.270 --> 12:40.280
<i>How should we attack it?</i>

12:40.930 --> 12:44.490
<i>For now, I'll do what I always do
 and draw its attention...</i>

12:46.990 --> 12:48.450
<i>and they'll attack from behind.</i>

12:52.200 --> 12:53.280
It blocked our attacks.

12:53.280 --> 12:57.540
But the crystal can only erect 
a barrier around itself.

13:00.960 --> 13:03.340
We can do this. Keep up the pressure.

13:07.120 --> 13:08.480
It blinded us?

13:08.480 --> 13:09.640
Is everyone okay?

13:11.020 --> 13:12.420
What's wrong, Marius?

13:12.420 --> 13:14.160
It's Lilia.

13:18.810 --> 13:21.270
Lilia's acting strange.

13:26.230 --> 13:28.410
What's wrong with you, Lilia?

13:28.410 --> 13:29.910
Stop...

13:30.680 --> 13:33.170
Stop hurting Lily!

13:34.720 --> 13:36.210
<i>I have to protect her.</i>

13:36.630 --> 13:37.830
Lily!

13:38.790 --> 13:41.130
You screwed up again.

13:41.130 --> 13:42.210
<i>I have to protect her.</i>

13:43.030 --> 13:45.350
<i>Stop hurting Lily.</i>

13:45.350 --> 13:48.300
<i>I have to protect Lily.</i>

13:50.380 --> 13:54.430
How dare you look at your father like that!

13:53.590 --> 14:00.400
<i>S-Someone, help...</i>

13:55.740 --> 13:58.120
You brats just get in the way.

14:03.770 --> 14:06.850
Don't hurt Lily anymore!

14:08.280 --> 14:09.950
Nin, cure her.

14:09.950 --> 14:10.620
Wait.

14:11.160 --> 14:13.700
The others have been afflicted 
with status effects, too.

14:14.140 --> 14:16.420
I'll cure these two first.

14:16.420 --> 14:17.330
Got it.

14:17.650 --> 14:22.920
<i>I see. Only Marius, Nin, and I are 
resistant to status effects.</i>

14:22.920 --> 14:26.590
<i>If we'd all been affected,
 our party could've been wiped out.</i>

14:29.550 --> 14:31.470
Life Conversion!

14:33.420 --> 14:36.020
You knocked the crystal away. Nice.

14:36.630 --> 14:39.450
Marius, can you keep 
the dark skeleton in check?

14:40.160 --> 14:42.860
On it. That'll be easier for me.

14:43.150 --> 14:43.960
Lilia!

14:50.550 --> 14:52.200
I'm sorry, Lilia.

14:55.790 --> 14:58.190
Calm down, Lilia.

14:55.790 --> 14:58.990
Let go. Stop hurting her.

14:58.990 --> 15:02.210
Stop hurting Lily!

15:03.670 --> 15:07.460
You mentioned your parents 
abandoned you and now you live together.

15:08.320 --> 15:15.810
Actually, it'd be more accurate to say 
we were being abused by them and ran away.

15:16.450 --> 15:19.770
<i>Is she seeing visions of her past trauma?</i>

15:20.830 --> 15:26.730
<i>A frenzied state can sometimes be calmed
by saying things to counteract the cause.</i>

15:27.150 --> 15:30.340
Lilia, there's no one here who 
would do harm to the two of you.

15:35.260 --> 15:38.960
Don't worry. You're both strong now.

15:45.100 --> 15:46.950
R-Rud?

15:47.360 --> 15:50.730
Yeah, it's me. We're all here for you.

15:51.550 --> 15:53.600
You can calm down now.

15:57.040 --> 16:00.390
No matter what happens, 
I will protect the two of you.

16:03.540 --> 16:05.510
I-I...

16:05.940 --> 16:09.580
You were just confused 
because of the dark skeleton's magic.

16:11.800 --> 16:13.070
It's okay.

16:13.430 --> 16:16.840
You have lots of people to help you now.

16:19.530 --> 16:24.000
Yeah, you're right. 
We have you and the others now.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.210
Marius, nice work hanging in there.

16:27.520 --> 16:29.510
Come back so we can heal you.

16:29.510 --> 16:32.420
This is a piece of cake, but sure.

16:33.040 --> 16:36.860
We can't fight properly 
unless we destroy the yellow one.

16:36.860 --> 16:39.970
But once we do that, it'll be easy.

16:42.800 --> 16:45.900
<i>It's not going to let me charge.
 In that case...</i>

16:45.900 --> 16:47.560
Nin. We need you.

16:50.850 --> 16:54.320
<i>This will provide me with some
 protection from its fire magic.</i>

16:58.640 --> 17:00.540
<i>The crystals respond quickly.</i>

17:00.810 --> 17:02.500
<i>It's not working.</i>

17:05.720 --> 17:09.670
Lilia. Marius. I may have
found a way to break through.

17:09.670 --> 17:12.090
The water droplets that were stuck to me

17:12.090 --> 17:14.800
flew threw the barrier and
 stuck to the dark skeleton.

17:15.320 --> 17:19.350
It probably can't block magical and 
physical attacks at the same time.

17:20.480 --> 17:22.220
It's worth a shot.

17:30.130 --> 17:32.210
The fire magic passed through the barrier.

17:32.820 --> 17:35.320
This is what you get for messing with me.

17:41.450 --> 17:45.830
It blocked our attacks, but we're 
making progress. Let's keep it up.

17:57.700 --> 18:01.470
Don't bother. That attack won't 
work on anyone here anymore.

18:02.160 --> 18:06.350
My spell is nullifying status effects.

18:09.920 --> 18:14.150
Luna's wind magic, Nin's water magic, 
and Lily's fire magic.

18:14.600 --> 18:16.110
It's impressive.

18:17.570 --> 18:21.740
The yellow crystal's glowing. It's planning 
to erect a barrier and try to escape.

18:22.910 --> 18:26.250
Rud, you'll get caught in our spells.

18:26.550 --> 18:30.920
I'll use Life Conversion to turn 
that damage into an attack.

18:33.960 --> 18:37.050
Life Conversion!

18:40.470 --> 18:42.500
That definitely weakened it.

18:49.810 --> 18:51.190
It split?

18:51.190 --> 18:53.240
There are more crystals, too.

18:56.190 --> 18:58.780
Lilia and Marius, take one of them down.

18:59.120 --> 19:01.400
But we don't know which is the real one.

19:01.400 --> 19:04.650
It doesn't matter. 
At this rate, they'll crush Rud.

19:06.850 --> 19:08.540
That's the real one.

19:27.310 --> 19:29.430
Its movements changed?

19:29.940 --> 19:30.940
In that case...

19:32.220 --> 19:34.730
This is the end!

19:39.290 --> 19:41.400
Marius and Lilia, get in there.

19:58.980 --> 20:02.510
I was worried when the 
boss suddenly appeared.

20:02.760 --> 20:05.470
I need a break after that.

20:05.680 --> 20:10.680
Yeah. Let's find the magic circle and
 take a break before proceeding.

20:10.920 --> 20:13.210
I'll use detection magic to look for it.

20:13.210 --> 20:16.650
There's no fog here, so it should work.

20:18.530 --> 20:19.290
Huh?

20:19.290 --> 20:20.030
What is it?

20:20.330 --> 20:24.110
I can't find it. I can't sense it at all.

20:25.130 --> 20:28.190
Does that mean this is the bottom floor?

20:29.330 --> 20:30.970
Marius, what do you think?

20:32.320 --> 20:38.290
Honestly, I'm not sure what this 
labyrinth's guardian is thinking.

20:38.520 --> 20:42.860
It's possible that dark skeleton 
was their masterpiece,

20:42.860 --> 20:46.370
and they fear us now 
because we defeated it.

20:46.370 --> 20:48.760
So they sealed off the route
 to the next level?

20:48.760 --> 20:52.980
Yeah. I've got a feeling 
this guardian is unusual.

20:53.440 --> 20:56.000
So this is as far as we can go, huh?

20:56.540 --> 20:59.940
We've accomplished plenty,
 so we'll head back.

21:03.630 --> 21:07.500
What's that? You're leaving?

21:11.340 --> 21:12.150
Who's there?

21:15.510 --> 21:19.460
<i>Who is this strangely imposing little girl?</i>

21:19.460 --> 21:21.230
Rud, this is bad.

21:25.070 --> 21:30.590
Hm, were more dark skeletons 
supposed to spawn here?

21:31.310 --> 21:35.310
<i>"Supposed to"? Ugh. We can't 
handle four at once right now.</i>

21:35.640 --> 21:38.220
I thought I'd removed them.

21:41.780 --> 21:43.280
A single attack...

21:43.690 --> 21:47.590
I wasn't expecting a demon king.
